PROBECTL COMMERCIAL SOURCE LICENSE

DRAFT-FOR-COUNSEL — NOT FINAL COMMERCIAL TERMS
License identifier: LicenseRef-Probectl-Commercial

IMPORTANT: This document is a drafting skeleton for counsel review. It does not
replace an order form, reseller agreement, support agreement, or other agreement
signed by the Licensor. Until counsel publishes final terms, production or
resale rights exist only when granted by a separately executed agreement with
the Licensor.

Copyright (c) the probectl contributors and applicable rights holders.
All rights not expressly granted are reserved.

1. Scope

This license applies only to source and related materials under the repository's
`ee/` directory (the "Commercial Software"). The MPL-2.0 license in the
repository root applies to core files outside `ee/`; it does not apply to the
Commercial Software.

2. Definitions

"Licensor" means [COUNSEL TO INSERT FINAL LEGAL ENTITY AND ADDRESS].

"Valid Commercial License" means an unexpired Enterprise or MSP entitlement
issued by the Licensor and used within its licensed customer, deployment,
feature, and tenant limits. A signed order form or other executed agreement—not
the visibility of this repository—controls the commercial scope.

"Production Use" means using the Commercial Software to operate, secure,
observe, manage, or support a live organization, customer, or service. It does
not include a time-limited internal evaluation that processes only synthetic or
non-production data.

"Resale" means providing a hosted, managed, sublicensed, or otherwise
commercially supplied service or product to a third party using the Commercial
Software, whether separately or bundled with other software.

3. Source review and licensed-use grant

3.1 Source review. Subject to this license, a recipient may view the Commercial
Software solely for evaluation, security review, interoperability assessment,
and deciding whether to acquire a Valid Commercial License. This limited review
permission grants no Production Use, distribution, or Resale right.

3.2 Licensed use. While the recipient holds a Valid Commercial License and
complies with the applicable executed agreement, the Licensor grants a limited,
non-exclusive, non-transferable right to reproduce, modify, and use the
Commercial Software solely for that recipient's licensed internal use. Copies
and modifications must retain this notice and remain subject to the same
commercial restrictions.

3.3 Evaluation. Any evaluation beyond source review—including executing the
Commercial Software—requires written evaluation terms from the Licensor. Those
terms define duration, data restrictions, and permitted environments.

4. Restrictions

Except where an executed agreement expressly says otherwise, a recipient may
not:

* use the Commercial Software in production without a Valid Commercial License;
* resell, host for third parties, provide managed services, sublicense, or
  distribute the Commercial Software without both an MSP entitlement and a
  separately executed reseller agreement;
* remove or obscure copyright, SPDX, trademark, or license notices;
* use the Commercial Software outside licensed feature, tenant, deployment, or
  customer limits;
* represent that repository access, source visibility, or a technical ability
  to bypass a feature gate grants commercial rights; or
* use probectl names, logos, or marks except as an executed trademark or
  reseller agreement permits.

